  "id": "Compound::DB00578 - Gene::9356",
  "verbalization": "Carbenicillin, a member of the penicillin class of antibiotics, is consistently linked to Slc22a6 through multiple pathways. The evidence suggests that Carbenicillin, as part of the broader penicillin family, binds to Slc22a6, a transporter protein involved in the uptake of various molecules, including drugs. This relationship is supported by the shared inclusion of Carbenicillin in Penicillins and its binding to Slc22a6 in multiple pathways, with the lowest common ancestor of Carbenicillin and its related compounds (Bacampicillin, Cloxacillin) also showing a connection to Slc22a6. The recurring mechanism involves the interaction of penicillin antibiotics with Slc22a6, likely through a common pathway that involves the inhibition of transporter activity. The evidence is robust and consistent across different pathways, suggesting a mechanistic link between Carbenicillin and Slc22a6 that is supported by the shared biological context of penicillin antibiotics and their interaction with transporters.",
